{"findings":[{"rule_id":"WPS-004","evidence":[{"kind":"dimension","ref":"D12","page":1,"quote":"⌀ 16 H7 (+0.018/0)"},{"kind":"title_block","ref":"surface_treatment","page":1,"quote":"I.Z.B.P. (TRIVALENT)"}],"comment":"The ⌀16 H7 hole (D12) has a tolerance band of 0.018 mm, but the drawing does not account for the added thickness of the I.Z.B.P. plating specified in the title block. Plating buildup inside the hole will reduce its diameter and can prevent the mating shaft from fitting; the designer should either specify that the hole be reamed after plating or adjust the pre-plate size to allow for the coating thickness."
    ,
    "recommended_correction": "Add a note specifying the hole is to be machined/reamed after plating, or adjust the pre-plate dimension to accommodate the I.Z.B.P. coating thickness."}]}
